1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:01,500
How many verbs about cooking

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,650
do you know?

3
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:04,889
Here are four.

4
00:00:04,889 --> 00:00:07,840
First, bring the sauce to the boil.

5
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,450
'Bring to'.

6
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:11,180
If you bring something to the boil,

7
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:14,590
then you heat it up until it bubbles.

8
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:16,619
Remember to put the direct object

9
00:00:16,619 --> 00:00:18,130
before 'to'.

10
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:20,222
Now, mix in some herbs.

11
00:00:20,222 --> 00:00:22,289
Using a spoon to combine the herbs

12
00:00:22,289 --> 00:00:25,470
with the sauce is called mixing in.

13
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:27,380
Then set aside to cool down.

14
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,300
Two verbs here.

15
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:31,319
'Set Aside' means 'to move

16
00:00:31,319 --> 00:00:32,450
something away from where you

17
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:35,430
are working and leave it alone'.

18
00:00:35,430 --> 00:00:37,250
If you cool something down,

19
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:38,800
its temperature reduces.

20
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,846
These last three are phrasal verbs.

21
00:00:40,846 --> 00:00:42,209
You can either put the direct

22
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:43,720
object in the middle of

23
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:45,376
the verb or at the end.

24
00:00:45,376 --> 00:00:47,300
So you can bring things to the

25
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,400
boil in a pan, mix them in

26
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,680
with a spoon and set them aside

27
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,504
by a window to cool down.

